# No SPA catch-all on purpose.
#
# This used to be `/*  /index.html  200`, which took the live site down: during a
# deploy a request for /assets/Landing-<hash>.js arrived before that file was in
# place, the catch-all answered with index.html — HTTP 200, Content-Type
# text/html — and Cloudflare cached that under the asset's own URL. Because
# /assets/* is served `immutable, max-age=31536000` (correct for content-hashed
# files), the wrong response stayed pinned at the edge, every dynamic import
# failed with "Failed to fetch dynamically imported module", and the page went
# blank. `_redirects` cannot express "fall back for pages but not for /assets/*",
# so the fallback goes away entirely.
#
# Nothing needs it: the app has no client-side router — App.tsx switches views in
# React state, so the only real URL is "/". Unknown paths now get a genuine 404
# instead of a 200 pretending to be an asset.
#
# If a router is ever added, do NOT just restore `/* /index.html 200` — deep
# links would work again, and so would this outage. Exclude /assets/* first.
